e_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:T1","usage":{"input_tokens":27381,"output_tokens":1980,"requests":3}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"34fc5e0065359bceb8379fa0754a2616b740975c552bc0f2503e9e14f096a38c"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:T3","usage":{"input_tokens":46115,"output_tokens":2761,"requests":5}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"ec7c46e875c9d87d3949e0180c317297101a341a75f2d83cfea0233a9f3e4e66"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:T5c","usage":{"input_tokens":56919,"output_tokens":2324,"requests":5}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"5e7011bd8b282e05295f4f6d302f8da14bd50e9346fe985401f8633815d0b42c"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:project.symbol-reference-completeness","usage":{"input_tokens":81373,"output_tokens":3077,"requests":7}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"453d662907246d49545bd04528a5e77961a750472c01fcc8066b73381058f6cc"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:T8","usage":{"input_tokens":137751,"output_tokens":3592,"requests":8}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"b7c117d4ed296f56d35ee371f844bc3591982c5bfed564fb29d489838b0d748c"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:G6","usage":{"input_tokens":115054,"output_tokens":5132,"requests":8}}],"version":1},"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Make the correlation-id read point explicit and reconcile it with the exported per-candidate span trace_ids: state where the 'active OTel span' is read (given rebar opens no root span, the boundary usually has none recording), and either scope the header/span-alignment in-scope claim to cases where a recording rebar span actually exists at read time, or justify how a boundary-read id aligns with the independently-rooted candidate spans that export to Langfuse.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.4,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'the correlation id is read from the active OpenTelemetry span when one is recording, minting only as fallback ... so an unrelated minted id would put a different id on the gateway header than on those spans — two traces for one run'","Plan concedes: 'rebar opens no root span, so a fanned-out gate run remains many traces rather than one'","Code: candidate spans open per-call with no rebar-owned root — tracing.py:183 `with candidate_span(...)` inside _TracedCandidateModel.request; candidate_span (tracing.py:89-101) calls trace.get_tracer(...).start_as_current_span with no explicit parent; search for start_span/get_current_span in src/rebar returns no rebar-owned root span opener","At the gate-run BOUNDARY (where run-correlation reads the id) the candidate spans have not yet opened, so there is no recording rebar span to read — the fallback mint path is taken, and the later per-candidate exported spans carry independent trace_ids"],"finding":"The in-scope claim that reading the correlation id from the active OTel span (minting only as fallback) makes the gateway header id match rebar's own exported Langfuse spans is not achieved by the described read point. rebar opens no root/gate-run span (the plan concedes this), and the id is read ONCE at the gate-run boundary — where no rebar-owned recording span exists — so it mints. The spans that actually export to Langfuse are the per-candidate spans (candidate_span, opened inside each model request() with no common parent at boundary time), each its own trace root; their trace_ids will not equal the minted/captured header value. The header-vs-span divergence the plan says it avoids therefore persists whenever there is fan-out.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fc6bbbe63c64bdaaf","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan section 'Out of scope' (the 'Sharing an id ... IS in scope' paragraph) and 'Child decomposition' run-correlation bullet ('read f